    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d307">

                <pb facs="0490" n="390" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg390"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/327½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-12-07">December 7,
                        1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>After reading the papers of the past three days, I am inclined to think that it
                    would be well to tell Davis, confidentially, something to this effect: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Now that the effect of denunciation by the Japanese has been made clear
                            to Matsudaira by both the British and ourselves, we think you should do
                            nothing further before December thirty-first, as a result <pb
                                facs="0491" n="391" xml:id="pg391"/> of which the Japanese could use
                            that as a reason or a partial reason for denunciation. In other words,
                            we are in an excellent position at the present time. Even if it involves
                            keeping the conversations going until December thirty-first, it is
                            worthwhile to do it in order that the whole onus of denunciation can be
                            placed on the Japanese without giving them any excuses.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>What do you think.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ranklin</hi>] D. R[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">oosevelt</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
